  "notes": "The London pianist who supplied a 2022 Kendrick album’s harmonic spine — postminimalist piano inside mainstream rap, and the only entry in this section whose defining feature is **the absence of drums**. His tracks are the drumless or late-entering material; where drums arrive they are sparse and half-time-feeling, after a full piano statement. Harmony is modal and slow-moving with pedal tones, added 9ths and 11ths, unresolved suspensions, and **genuine motion over 8+ bars rather than a loop** — the longest chord durations in the roster. Piano left hand carries the low end; there is no 808 on his own contributions. ⚠ `medium`: the harmonic approach and role are documented, tempo values necessarily approximate `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ A progression family authored `Imaj7`, which `Numeral::parse` cannot read — it knows i, VI, bII and vii° and takes the seventh from `chords.extensions`, not from the numeral. An unreadable numeral makes the generator skip the slot, so that whole family produced NO CHORDS AT ALL, and chords.rs caught it only when a seed happened to pick it. Now `I`; the major-7th colour is carried by the extensions block, where it was always meant to be.",
